    "law": "For acceleration A with no binding speed cap, equating x_truck = 15t and x_car = At²/2 gives the positive meeting time t = 30/A. With A = 2 m/s² this is 15 s, at which the car reaches 30 m/s. If the car accelerates to a cap V with 15 < V < 30 m/s and then maintains V, its position thereafter is Vt - V²/(2A), giving t = V²/[2A(V - 15)].",
